WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.888
Before moving into the assignment exercises use this
slide as a quick

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:09.312
self-check Try to answer each question without
running code first Why is

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:13.962
an explicit column list usually better than SELECT
star Because it makes

00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:17.550
the intended output clear and avoids returning data
you do not need

00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:23.550
What is wrong with discharge_date equals NULL NULL
is not tested with

00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:29.125
ordinary equality Use discharge_date IS NULL Why

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.025
should LIMIT usually be paired with ORDER BY when
the result has

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.112
a meaning such as newest or oldest Because LIMIT
alone does not

00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:40.062
guarantee which rows come first What should you do
before a new

00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:44.050
UPDATE or DELETE Run a SELECT with the same WHERE
condition and

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:48.725
inspect the target rows What is the difference
between COMMIT and ROLLBACK

00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:55.100
COMMIT keeps the transaction's changes ROLLBACK
discards them If

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:57.912
you can explain these answers in your own words that
is more

00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:02.450
important than memorizing the exact wording on the
slide If one question

00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:05.600
is still unclear go back to the related example and
run it

00:01:05.612 --> 00:01:10.175
again SQL concepts become much easier when you
connect the rule with

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.225
a visible result
